  "reclassification_note": "Mechanical LIKELY BINARY (stage b) is a ratio-rule mislabel on two zeros: odd 0.0027% vs even 0.0001% ('96% apart' of nothing; deepest fold dip 2.6% of the BLS depth = evaporation, the TIC 294671640 / 299900306 pattern), and stage (c) independently finds no binary (no eclipse pair, quadrature delta -0.003% at -1.4 sigma). Not a phantom either: the event duration is 0.72 h (odd/even estimator-blind, third such case this sweep), and BOTH pipeline stitches measure a positive fixed-ephemeris excess (cap-20 +0.106% +/- 0.014%, median event depth = full BLS depth; uncapped +0.045% +/- 0.008% spread across all three era groups). But the depth is not constant (cap-20 chi2 p = 2e-5), halves between stitches, and the uncapped periodogram demotes the peak (14.5007 d, SDE 9.2). Era-spread shallow variability on the patch's brightest M dwarf; the planet reading is closed by the uncapped check, the phantom reading is forbidden by the two-stitch excess. Grey drawer.",
